# A hand-written stand-in for a real commit log (see issue #34), in the
# core port event language timeball/core_port_trace.hpp reads: I retires instructions,
# L and S load and store. examples/transcript_replay.cpp reads this file
# and replays it, unchanged, against two chip graphs.
#
# The shape: five passes over the same four 64-byte lines — a loop touching
# a small working set repeatedly, the pattern that tells apart a cache that
# holds it from one that does not.
I 5
L 0x0000
L 0x0040
L 0x0080
L 0x00c0
I 5
L 0x0000
L 0x0040
L 0x0080
L 0x00c0
I 5
L 0x0000
L 0x0040
L 0x0080
L 0x00c0
I 5
L 0x0000
L 0x0040
L 0x0080
L 0x00c0
I 5
L 0x0000
L 0x0040
L 0x0080
L 0x00c0
